&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Platform Engineer to join our AI Technology team and play a critical role in ensuring the stability and scalability of the firm’s internal Agentic AI platform. This is a high-impact, hands-on engineering position where you’ll contribute code, automation workflows, observability, metrics, and support users as issues arise. You’ll work in a dynamic, fast-paced environment where product requirements evolve, and business stakeholders are deeply engaged.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will set the reliability standards for Enterprise AI, defining Service Level Objectives (SLOs), error budgets, and custom incident response runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will own the observability, incident response, reliability, and scalability of our AI platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that our agents, gateways, LLM proxies, and RAG pipelines operate with high availability, accuracy, and financial efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support users in a dedicated help channel when issues arise — investigating root causes, providing solutions, monitoring the status of upstream dependencies, and communicating updates back to users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll also be involved in the team’s code quality and best practices, identify gaps in development lifecycles, and continuously improve both the core platform and how developers build with it.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you need:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional cloud automation or site reliability engineering experience, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development best practices and experience creating applications in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working creating and integrating REST APIs, and event-driven and asynchronous architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with both relational (Postgres, MySQL) and NoSQL databases (DynamoDB, Elastic Search)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS cloud services (S3, OpenSearch, DynamoDB, etc.), Kubernetes-driven deployments, Github Actions, and modern CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for AI, creative ideas for how it can be a tool for problem solving and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A thoughtful approach to problem-solving; ability to break down complex issues methodically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills; Able to translate technical concepts for non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’d love if you had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing agentic AI applications, harnesses, MCP servers, and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with or experience building AI agents, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines, or agentic tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability tooling such as DataDog&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an AI Platform Lead to lead the strategy, architecture, engineering, and operation of the firm’s shared AI technology platform. You will build the foundations that enable research, investment, and business teams to develop and deploy AI applications securely, reliably, and at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical leadership role combining platform ownership, architectural direction, and team leadership. You will own the AI platform roadmap and oversee delivery across model access and serving, agent frameworks, enterprise connectivity, developer tooling, evaluation, observability, and supporting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with AI application engineers, quantitative researchers, portfolio managers, infrastructure, cybersecurity, and technology leadership, you will translate business priorities into reusable platform capabilities that accelerate delivery while maintaining strong engineering and operational standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Strategy and Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the firm’s AI platform strategy and roadmap, aligning investments with research, investment, and operational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the platform lifecycle, from technology evaluation and architecture through implementation, adoption, and ongoing operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead build-versus-buy decisions across a rapidly evolving vendor landscape, balancing capability, integration requirements, cost, and operational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear platform priorities, service ownership, and measures of success across adoption, reliability, developer productivity, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture and Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end architecture for shared AI services, including model gateways, inference, agent runtimes, orchestration, retrieval, and enterprise data integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of agent frameworks, developer tooling, MCP servers and gateways, and reusable tools, plugins, and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reference architectures, APIs, engineering standards, and deployment patterns that support interoperability, scalability, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide infrastructure decisions across cloud, on-premises, and hybrid environments, including Kubernetes and GPU-backed workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain hands-on in critical design decisions, prototyping, code reviews, and complex implementation challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability, Security, and Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure platform services meet defined expectations for availability, performance, resilience, and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed authentication, authorization, entitlements, secrets management, and data-access controls throughout the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build evaluation and observability capabilities that make AI applications and agents testable, traceable, and safe to release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standards for automated testing, CI/CD, versioning, dependency management, and software supply-chain security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cybersecurity, risk, and compliance teams to support auditability, appropriate human oversight, and controlled access to sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership and Platform Adoption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and mentor a high-performing AI platform engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction, prioritize delivery, and establish clear accountability across platform components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with AI application teams to turn recurring solution patterns into reusable, production-ready platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat internal engineering teams as platform customers, providing effective documentation, onboarding, tooling, and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical trade-offs, delivery progress, and investment recommendations to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive standardization and automation to reduce technical debt, operational risk, and infrastructure complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in software engineering, platform engineering, infrastructure, or distributed systems, including senior technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading engineering teams and owning shared platforms or infrastructure used by multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of taking complex technical capabilities from initial design through production deployment and ongoing operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of LLMs, agentic systems, retrieval-augmented generation, model serving, and AI application architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on software development expertise, particularly in Python, and the ability to evaluate designs and contribute to critical implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with distributed systems, APIs, Kubernetes, containerization, cloud or hybrid infrastructure, and infrastructure automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of reliability engineering, observability, cybersecurity, identity, and access management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical judgment, prioritization, and communication skills, with the ability to influence senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a related technical discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in hedge funds, quantitative investment management, trading, or financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building enterprise AI platforms, internal developer platforms, or shared services with broad organizational adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with agent frameworks, MCP servers and gateways, AI evaluation, and MLOps/LLMOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with high-performance computing, NVIDIA GPU infrastructure, and inference optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing technology vendors, platform budgets, and infrastructure costs.&lt;/li&gt;
