&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking to hire an exceptional individual to join our Legal Team at Schonfeld. You will have the opportunity to work within two of the Legal Team’s practice areas: Portfolio Management (PM onboarding/offboarding/counseling) and Capital Development &amp;amp; Investor Relations. This is a dynamic opportunity to partner with senior management and to blend your legal acumen with your desire to get closer to the business while addressing a wide variety of legal issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary focus will be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting, negotiating and interpreting various contracts directly with our portfolio managers (most commonly, investment management agreements, employment agreements and deeds), as well as handling related onboarding and offboarding matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All facets of fund formation and capital development, including launching new investor-facing products, updating existing fund documents, preparing and reviewing side letters, maintaining fund side letter logs, negotiating placement agent agreements, and assisting with investor queries and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to spearhead strategic transactions, private equity transactions, loan documents and regulatory matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering closely with our stakeholders in other departments in furtherance of the above goals, including the Firm’s CEO/CIO, COO and CFO, as well as the strategy heads, business development teams and our capital development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working collaboratively with outside counsel and other advisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A J.D. from an accredited law school and admittance to a state bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 4-6 years of experience in the investment management/funds practice area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience is preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior legal analytical and drafting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior organization, communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and handle urgent competing workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a demanding, fast-paced and fluid environment while maintaining superior rigor and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and maintain positive working relationships with internal and external stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest or experience in identifying and implementing AI tools to assist the legal team more broadly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
