&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking to hire an exceptional Director, Central Compliance &amp;amp; Europe (“EU”) Regulatory Liaison, to join our London office. Reporting to the Deputy Chief Compliance Officer, this senior leader will manage a team of 3–4 compliance officers and hold responsibility for multiple Centers of Excellence (CoEs) within the firm&#39;s Central Compliance organization, spanning Financial Crime, Policy Management, and Core Compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to leading these global CoEs, the role serves as the firm&#39;s senior point of contact for EU regulatory matters in each jurisdiction where Schonfeld is licensed or authorized. The position requires a strong combination of technical compliance expertise, operational and process discipline, and the proactive use of AI and technology to drive efficiency across the function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the firm&#39;s UK and larger EU Regulatory Liaison function, overseeing in-country Compliance Officers who act as SMEs and points of contact for local regulators, manage the local regulatory change agenda, and scope local requirements into the CoEs; sign off on local filings and registrations and engage in the expansion efforts of offices across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide overall management, supervision, and strategic vision for multiple CoEs within Central Compliance, setting priorities, resourcing, and hiring plans, and adapting program design to regulatory and business change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and develop a team of 3–4 compliance officers, providing leadership, mentorship, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the firm&#39;s Global/Regional AML Program, the Investor PEP/Sanctions screening process, and all AML/financial crime-related regulatory filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the firm&#39;s Global Compliance Policies &amp;amp; Procedures framework, including standardized P&amp;amp;P templates, the P&amp;amp;P Review Program, and regulator/client-facing policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer the Code of Ethics Program end-to-end – including PA Dealing, Gifts &amp;amp; Entertainment, Outside Business Interests, and Political Contributions – alongside Conflicts Management, Compliance Training, Licensing &amp;amp; Registrations, Certifications, and Employee Administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the adoption of AI and compliance technology to streamline workflows, reduce manual effort, and scale program delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral and collaborative member of the London Compliance Team and the broader global Compliance department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent; advanced degree (JD, MBA) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prrogressive compliance experience within financial services, with meaningful exposure to asset management, hedge funds, or investment advisory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership across multiple compliance disciplines (AML/financial crime, policy management, core compliance) with direct engagement with EU regulators such as the FCA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people management experience leading high-performing compliance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical knowledge of AML/financial crime regulation (FATF, EU AML Directives, UK POCA, US BSA/AML), PEP/sanctions frameworks, Code of Ethics programs, and conflicts management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong management, operational, and process-improvement skills with a track record of designing scalable, repeatable compliance processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage credibly with regulators, senior management, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and judgment skills, with the ability to navigate ambiguity, assess risk, and escalate appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Firm and team first in thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love if you had:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previously held SMF16/17 designation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating within or leading a Center of Excellence or center-led compliance model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to leverage AI tools and compliance technology platforms (e.g. Microsoft Copilot, Power Automate, or similar) to enhance program efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certifications such as CAMS, ICA Diploma, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the multi-manager or alternative investment management model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory engagement and change management across multiple EU jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
