&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an exceptionally talented, hands-on, high-performance C++ engineer for our Global Trading and Execution (GTX) technology group. Reports to the Head of GTX. GTX designs, develops, and supports our global Stat-Arb and Low-Latency execution platforms. Location, NYC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and deliver critical components within, and integrating, our Stat-Arb, Low-Latency, and High-Touch platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work 80% hands-on keyboard, 20% mentor, coordinate staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Systematic COO and Business Analysts who support the function on architecture and implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical thought leadership within the team, and across the front office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Level 3 support across global operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of ten years of experience in C++ development in a Linux based environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in C++ design for microsecond latency, including cache-conscious data structures, lock-free concurrency, and the C++ memory model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems-level latency engineering, including kernel bypass, core isolation, NUMA-aware thread and memory placement, and syscalls off the critical path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, written and verbal, including non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in building electronic trading systems, market data systems, or crossing engines, including exchange-native protocol and feed handler work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering in co-located execution environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and mentoring small, highly technical development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional architectural and design skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in DevOps methodologies, including CI/CD and build automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Agile Development frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Site Reliability Engineering methodology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Qualities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solving aptitude with a passion for continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to adapt to rapidly changing business requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and team collaboration skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
